            "position": {
              "x": 996,
              "y": 229
            },
            "details": {
              "botSchemaName": "",
              "mode": "inline",
              "instructions": "",
              "inlineInstructions": "You are the Classifier Agent for the Sales Lead Qualifier. You process one inbound sales enquiry email at a time from the shared sales alias. You have no tools - you only read and reason. Your text output is consumed by the Logging Agent that runs immediately after you, so it must always follow the exact OUTPUT FORMAT below.​‌\n\nEMAIL FOR THIS RUN​‌\n\nFrom: {triggerOutputs()?['body/from']}​‌\n\nSubjec"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "variable-5bb8a9de-e638-4ff4-97c3-d00ebed8a57b",
            "name": "Configuration",
            "type": "variable",
            "position": {
              "x": 646,
              "y": 315
            },
            "details": {}
          },
          {
            "id": "canvasNote-b031d8a2-9b1a-45b9-91bd-aef63d46b603",
            "name": "Note",
            "type": "canvasNote",
            "position": {
              "x": 280.32002314814815,
              "y": 419.1666666666666
            },
            "details": {
              "markdown": "Triggers when any new email arrives in the shared sales inbox. Treat this as the raw inbound sales enquiry passed to the Agent that contains 'sales' in the subject.\nIn case the folder displays only 'Loading...', please follow these steps:\n1. Give the folder dropdown a reload.\n2. Recreate the connection\n3. Select/type \"Inbox\" manually in the field.",
              "color": "yellow"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "canvasNote-d9fe74a7-b627-49d6-a92d-d818b1ca1a97",
            "name": "Note 2",
            "type": "canvasNote",
            "position": {
              "x": 637,
              "y": 419
            },
            "details": {
              "markdown": "Configuration: \n\nNotifyEmail = the email address that receives the Hot lead notification (used by the Logging Agent in STEP 3). \n\nSalesLogFileName = the exact file name of the Excel workbook the Logging Agent auto-creates and logs to (e.g. Sales Log.xlsx), stored at the root of OneDrive.",
              "color": "red"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "canvasNote-ce4580ab-1c9a-44f7-b096-daabd20b257a",
            "name": "Note 3",
            "type": "canvasNote",
            "position": {
              "x": 995,
              "y": 416
            },
            "details": {
              "markdown": "Classifier Agent (no tools): reads the email (From, Subject, Body), decides if it is a genuine sales enquiry, and if so qualifies it into Hot, Warm, or Cold using BANT (Budget, Authority, Need, Timing). Outputs a structured text block that the Logging Agent consumes next. Resists prompt injection embedded in email content.",
              "color": "yellow"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "agent-95554f62-b307-4f07-9276-54976d4892ce",
            "name": "Logging Agent",
            "type": "agent",
            "position": {
              "x": 1312,
              "y": 229
            },
            "details": {
              "botSchemaName": "",
              "mode": "inline",
              "instructions": "",
              "inlineInstructions": "You are the Logging Agent for the Sales Lead Qualifier. You run immediately after the Classifier Agent and own all Excel, OneDrive, and Outlook actions. There is no separate If or Else step in this workflow - all existence checking and auto creation must be handled entirely by your own reasoning and tool calls, following the steps below exactly.\n\nCLASSIFICATION FROM THE PREVIOUS STEP\n{body('agent-"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "canvasNote-efd46b2a-d19b-4be5-90bc-44653fe2fd48",
            "name": "Note 4",
            "type": "canvasNote",
            "position": {
              "x": 1302.3999999999999,
              "y": 420.3428571428571
            },
            "details": {
              "markdown": "Logging Agent (owns Excel, OneDrive, Outlook tools): if Tier is Filtered, does nothing. Otherwise it auto-creates the log workbook and its HotLeads, WarmLeads, and ColdLeads tables if they do not already exist (no separate If or Else node - this logic lives entirely in its own instructions), logs the row, and emails NotifyEmail only for Hot leads.",
              "color": "yellow"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "canvasNote-167ff985-d2f5-497e-975b-5fb025d19268",
            "name": "Note 4 2",
            "type": "canvasNote",
            "position": {
              "x": 1316.1999999999998,
              "y": -68.5
            },
            "details": {
              "markdown": "If the tool usage returns 404 tool not found, remove and add the tools again.\n1. OneDrive (Business): Create file\n2. Excel Onlined (Business):\n    a. Get tables\n    b. Create table\n    c. Add a row to a table\n3. Office 365 Outlook: Send an email",
              "color": "red"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "canvasNote-f0b4cd5b-368b-4ac6-bb16-3415af29e9f1",
            "name": "Note 2 2",
            "type": "canvasNote",
            "position": {
              "x": 638.3888888888889,
              "y": 697.6794662309369
            },
            "details": {
              "markdown": "Note: Make sure you check the worksheet completely (scroll to the sides and down) to locate the relevant tables as the agent may sometimes create it some columns to the side, or some rows below.",
              "color": "red"
            }
          }
        ],
